          "book_page": 210,
          "pdf_page": 218,
          "locator": "Example 4.1.8 (Borel's paradox): the naive expectation that longitude and great-circle angle are both uniform; only the longitude is"
        },
        {
          "path": "source/references/durrett-probability-2019-01-11/PTE5_011119.pdf",
          "sha256": "aeac36cbf5e44c53d69fa60a2d29a393e2d0e8c955ee103bd845d925fd910886",
          "book_page": 210,
          "pdf_page": 218,
          "locator": "resolution: the angle is independent of the longitude in either parametrization, so the conditional law equals the unconditional one, nonuniform because more of the sphere lies near the equator than near the pole"
        }
